  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Elevated Technologies Services reported $78.3M in contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Elevated Technologies Services received 28 awards so far this fiscal year, with an average award size of $2.8M, and obligations are down 74.8% year over year. Elevated Technologies Services shows a history of year-by-year obligations that includes $36.4M in FY22, $67.9M in FY23, $51.1M in FY24, $68.3M in FY25, and $311M in FY26. Elevated Technologies Services is concentrated with a single dominant buyer: the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $75.8M this fiscal year. Elevated Technologies Services sells primarily in the Other Building Equipment Contractors market, where obligations total $73.2M this fiscal year, followed by Facilities Support Services at $4.5M and Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance at $659K. Elevated Technologies Services also shows smaller obligations from the General Services Administration at $2.6M and from the Department of Justice at $7.2K, while the Department of the Interior shows $0 in obligations.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are the main customers of Elevated Technologies Services right now?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs is the main customer, obligating $75.8M in FY2027 to date. The General Services Administration obligated $2.6M and the Department of Justice obligated $7.2K. The Department of the Interior shows $0 in obligations."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services does Elevated Technologies Services provide to the government?",
        "body": "Other Building Equipment Contractors is the largest market for Elevated Technologies Services at $73.2M in FY2027 to date. Facilities Support Services follows at $4.5M, and Commercial and Industrial Machinery and Equipment Repair and Maintenance accounts for $659K. The company’s award profile this fiscal year includes 28 awards with an average award size of $2.8M."
      }
    ]
